+## Sales import and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time zone,
+  `qty` a whole number of dishes) and answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`:
+  the tickets imported and the dishes sold on them (the sum of `qty`).
+  Tickets imported before are skipped and not counted. One bad row
+  (`bad_request`) or an item running out (`sale_not_enough_stock`) and
+  nothing from the file is imported; the message names the row by its line
+  in the file (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one
+  `{ itemId, theoretical, actual, difference }` per item where either use is
+  above zero; `difference` is `actual - theoretical`.
